# `''` in a verbatim string: no escapes there, so the fix switches quotes.
mode: syntax
---- query
from 'orders.csv' | where customerId != @'it''s'
---- expected
PROGRAM@0..49
  PIPELINE@0..48
    IDENT@0..4 "from"
    WHITESPACE@4..5 " "
    LITERAL@5..17
      STRING@5..17 "'orders.csv'"
    WHITESPACE@17..18 " "
    PIPE@18..19 "|"
    WHITESPACE@19..20 " "
    WHERE_OP@20..48
      IDENT@20..25 "where"
      WHITESPACE@25..26 " "
      BIN_EXPR@26..48
        NAME_REF@26..36
          IDENT@26..36 "customerId"
        WHITESPACE@36..37 " "
        NEQ@37..39 "!="
        WHITESPACE@39..40 " "
        LITERAL@40..48
          STRING@40..45 "@'it'"
          STRING@45..48 "'s'"
  WHITESPACE@48..49 "\n"

error[DS0117]: `''` does not put a quote in a string
  --> query:1:45
  |
1 | from 'orders.csv' | where customerId != @'it''s'
  |                                             ^^ this ends the string and starts another
  |
  = help: a verbatim string has no escapes; use the other quote: `@"it's"`

with the machine-applicable fixes applied:
    from 'orders.csv' | where customerId != @"it's"
which parses without errors
